Package: gridmapper
Title: Allocate Geographic Features to Grid Cartograms
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Maintainer", "Name", , "maintainer@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "TODO: replace with the R package maintainer"),
    person("Dany", "Laksono", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "Author of the original 'gridmapper' JavaScript library")
  )
Description: Allocates geographic points or polygons to the cells of a
    rectangular or hexagonal grid by solving a mixed integer programme that
    minimises displacement from geographic position, with a compactness
    parameter controlling how tightly features cluster. Supports automatic
    estimation of grid dimensions, compactness and PCA rotation, spacer
    cells, adjacency rewards, simulated annealing post-processing, and
    Dorling and Demers cartograms. A port of the 'gridmapper' JavaScript
    library, itself inspired by Jo Wood's grid map allocation method.
